The Power of Thoughts - Thoughts as Energy-Rich Entities


What enormous benefit or harm our thoughts can cause


We usually pay little attention to our thoughts. We cannot see them, consider them insignificant, and science presents them as the result of brain waves that cannot have any consequences beyond the head. But in reality, thoughts do extend far beyond our bodies. They not only influence our own well-being and even our fate, but they also determine the quality of our relationships. And that's not all: As the creators of these high-energy structures, the quality of our thoughts also contributes even more to peace or unrest in the world than we think - without us being aware of it!


With just a little effort, we can find out what far-reaching effect our thoughts really have - we just have to pay a little attention to them! In this way, we can see in small ways how dark or aggressive thoughts can ruin our whole day, and if they persist for a long time, they can even make us grumpy, sullen and ill. Conversely, they can also make life much more beautiful, for example when you are newly in love!


But that's not all: people we approach with strong reservations or with good thoughts sense this and react accordingly. They either feel burdened and oppressed by us, or, conversely, accepted and encouraged. Of course, this plays a decisive role in whether they then approach us with sympathy or antipathy. Therefore, the quality of our relationships is very closely linked to the type and quality of our thoughts!


And ultimately, our fate is shaped by our thoughts and attitudes. So we have an incredible amount of control over things ourselves!


Below, important questions about the effectiveness of thoughts are answered. Did you know:


that the far-reaching impact of our thoughts was already known thousands of years ago, far more so than today?


that besides thoughts there are other, invisible and immeasurable phenomena that are highly effective?


that many of the mysteries of science can only be explained by assuming a world beyond our five senses?


why thoughts are highly energetic entities with enormous reach?


how terror, massacres and all other problems in this world are connected to such thoughts?


how we can therefore achieve a better world and more mature attitudes?



Why Thoughts Are Powerful Forces


... and how the nature of our thoughts determines the quality of our lives


Watch your thoughts, for they become words.
Watch your words, for they become actions.
Watch your actions, for they become habits. Watch
your habits, for they become your character.
Watch your character, for it becomes your destiny.


This quotation from the Talmud, which is thousands of years old, refers to the chain of consequences that follows natural law and begins with thoughts . It is hard to put the event more succinctly and accurately, and if we want to take it seriously, we face the great challenge, especially in our culture, of fundamentally changing and expanding our relationship and perspective on thoughts.


We still mostly see them as "smoke and mirrors", or actually even less than nothing! We usually perceive thinking itself as our private pleasure, to which we can indulge undisturbed and without consequences.


The saying "Thoughts are free!" can also be viewed from two sides: in the best case as the possibility of inner freedom, which no one can easily take away from us once we have achieved it, but in the unfavorable sense as the right to be able to think anything we want, even harmful things, without being prosecuted by anyone for it.


The claim that thoughts are powerful forces is not taken very seriously by most people, because most people assume that our thoughts are the product of our brain waves. In this case, it is logical to assume that these tiny energy flows take place exclusively in our own heads and cannot have any influence on the outside. This would make them "duty-free" in every respect. This is the materialistic view that is widespread in our country , which assumes that there is simply nothing apart from the world that we can see and measure . But if we want to get closer to the way thoughts work, there is no way around dealing with these invisible, subtle levels - because not being able to see this world and also thoughts does not prove that they do not exist and that they do not work!


The materialistic picture is currently being increasingly shattered by advances in science and by researchers who are choosing new, alternative approaches. Countless observations in a wide variety of areas, which cannot simply be ignored as non-existent, raise considerable doubts about the previous way of looking at things. More and more knowledge is being gained that suggests the existence of higher-level laws and a world beyond our five senses. But if we are ready to consider this finer, otherworldly world as a possibility, we are taking the first steps into the area in which our thoughts also form and are located!



To name a few examples:


All of the fundamental laws of creation elude any direct and measurable perception. However, we experience their effects every single second, and they determine all processes in this world, the smallest and the largest. No science would be practical without these underlying laws.  


The English biologist Rupert Sheldrake has discovered, among other things, that animals have amazing, almost telepathic abilities, which are reported here .

The scientist Albert Popp has proven that living cells emit photons, i.e. light. This light could cause the mysterious coordination of around a trillion ordered metabolic processes that take place in our bodies every second.

Thanatology (death research) has encountered numerous cases of unusual perceptions of clinically dead people that cannot be explained by conventional means.

Reincarnation research, on the other hand, has made many observations that compellingly suggest a transition of consciousness from a body that has died to a new body, i.e. a rebirth .


Last but not least, our free will , which allows us to make all the decisions in our lives, eludes any visibility and measurability even more than our thoughts.



